	(text "State: 0 T_IDLE, 1 T_SETUP, 2 T_WAIT, 3 T_CAPTURE (read), 4 T_HOLD (write), 5 T_RELEASE, 6 T_DONE.\nRead: SETUP asserts nCE/nOE; WAIT until counter==WAIT_READ; CAPTURE latches data and asserts ACK; HOLD releases nOE; RELEASE releases nCE; DONE.\nWrite: SETUP asserts nCE/nWE; WAIT until counter==WAIT_WRITE; HOLD raises nWE and asserts ACK; RELEASE raises nCE; DONE.  No nOE during write."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 350 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9cef1e40-d4ff-4d32-8fef-25b4188b8c5b")
	)

	(text "Wait-state formula: WAIT_READ = ceil((max(tAA,tCE,tOE)+margin)/Tclk); WAIT_WRITE = ceil((tWP+tDH+margin)/Tclk).\nDefault examples: 6264 read/write = 2/2; 28C256 read = 3; 27C512 read = 2. The 74HC161 free-runs and is cleared in T_SETUP; the 74HC688 compares the count with the WE-selected wait value.  Its P=R output is active-low, so U12B inverts WAIT_MATCH_N to the active-high WAIT_MATCH used by the microcode ROM. The 74HC688 outputs are active-low.  S02 is the only timing controller; REQ/WE are driven by the S11 bus fabric.  The MEM_DATA <-> DATA data path is provided by S04 U36 (74HC245), so this sheet no longer has a data transceiver."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 365 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "166f4234-7f6d-406d-992f-4157f7d3976d")
	)

	(embedded_fonts no)
)
